# 1.4 Attack Surface

An attack surface is the collection of interfaces, components and processes through which an adversary may influence or compromise a system.

For ML, the attack surface can include:

### Data layer

- public datasets;
- uploaded documents;
- scraped web data;
- user-generated content;
- labels;
- metadata;
- data pipelines.

### Training layer

- training scripts;
- feature engineering;
- hyperparameters;
- dependencies;
- GPUs;
- distributed training infrastructure.

### Model layer

- model weights;
- checkpoints;
- model configuration;
- tokenizers;
- adapters;
- quantized models.

### Application layer

- APIs;
- chat interfaces;
- mobile applications;
- web applications;
- agent tools.

### Operational layer

- CI/CD;
- model registries;
- cloud storage;
- secrets;
- monitoring;
- logging.

